Attributions:

- The shared-memory SPSC ring (libs/shm/include/raikiri/shm/spsc_ring.hpp)
  derives its layout — padded head/tail indices with process-private cached
  counterpart indices — from rigtorp::SPSCQueue by Erik Rigtorp
  (https://github.com/rigtorp/SPSCQueue, MIT license). Reimplemented for
  placement in shared memory across processes.

- The broadcast ring's per-slot versioning follows the LMAX Disruptor
  (https://lmax-exchange.github.io/disruptor/) single-writer sequencing
  design, adapted with seqlock-style validated reads.

- Architectural inspiration: nautilus_trader
  (https://github.com/nautechsystems/nautilus_trader, LGPL-3.0 — design
  patterns referenced, no code copied).
